    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0532" n="430" xml:id="pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Belgium/145a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Belgium</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-03T13:00:00-05:00">October 3, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Commander B. M. Thompson, a representative of the Treasury Department, will
                    visit Brussels in the near future to discuss question of obtaining cooperation
                    in preventing shipments of alcohol from Belgium destined for smuggling into
                    United States.</p>
                <p>Please extend appropriate assistance and inform consular officers at Antwerp and
                    Rotterdam.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
